Z||000000||mrgone||06-17-2001||11:34 PM||||started to take apart my dash to see if i could get some of those guaged to work<BR>got the back cover off, the lower cover off, the faceplate off switches out....<BR>couldnt fit my wratched down there to get the clear plastic off. and then i got stumped, how do i get in there? where are the grounds for the oil and coolent gauges?<BR>do i need to get in there ?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Devotshka||06-18-2001||12:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrgone:<BR><B>couldnt fit my wratched down there to get the clear plastic off. and then i got stumped, how do i get in there? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The guage cluster comes out as a unit (plastic/glass attached).  If i recall there are two 10mm bolts behind it on a metal flange holding it down.  Once you get those out the whole gauge assembly should lift back and out.  Just be sure to unplug your harnesses and if the light switches/power trunk etc are loomed through it, that they are separated.<BR>Once it is out, you can unscrew the plastic 'glass' and the black bezel to get at your gauges.||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||06-18-2001||01:23 AM||||there are also two bolts on the bottom. I modified mine so I could take out the plastic cover and get to my guages without taking out the whole thing||||reg||1
